            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0224" n="108" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/746.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires at London to the
                        Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 31, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Foreign Office intend to reply to Japan that although the British Government
                    can not undertake absolutely to prevent their nationals from making loans in
                    future, the Government are ready to “use their influence as far as possible to
                    prevent” such financial assistance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
